<H1>Motorcycle Trips and Pictures</H1>
<BR>
<a href="motorcycle_cascade_sr542.html"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_mtbaker_artist_point_20200921_2_road_sm.jpg"></A><BR><BR>
For a sucessfull trip the most important part is to <A HREF="motorcycle_prep.html">prepare for the trip</A> in advance of the trip.
<BR><BR>
While listening to the radio I heard a <A HREF="https://www.npr.org/programs/invisibilia/" target="_blank">Invisibilia podcast</A> on <A HREF="https://www.wabe.org/invisibilia-the-great-narrative-escape-slow-tv/" target="_blank">Norwegian 'Slow TV'</A>. The podcast inspired me to create some <A HREF="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slow_television" target="_blank">Slow TV</A> motorcycle rides:
<ul style="list-style-type:circle">
	<li>Riding around <A HREF="https://youtu.be/S-urMn_r1MQ" target="_blank">Moscow Idaho and Elk City</a> about 9+ hours May of 2021, this <A HREF="https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1j0hkklh5iRR2ky1TJ7WIs03VFewkg0zp" target="_blank">map shows the route</A>.</li>
	<li>Riding <A HREF="https://youtu.be/dJUagXAQT5s" target="_blank">Highway 101 (Part 1)</a> down the west coast, classic ride May 2020 and October 2021 (two rides spliced together), 12 hours (YouTube's maximum length). This <A HREF="https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=156dW0EfDXAVXDjeAWqzVYP7zBKBWC4Jt" target="_blank">map shows the route</A>.</li>
	<li>Riding <A HREF="https://youtu.be/o4HFLt0s_Yo" target="_blank">Highway 101 (Part 2)</a> up the west coast, classic ride October 7th and 8th, 2021 about 8 hours. This <A HREF="https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=156dW0EfDXAVXDjeAWqzVYP7zBKBWC4Jt" target="_blank">map shows the route</A>.</li>
	<li>Riding from <A HREF="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aVU8c6p0PCk" target="_blank">Spokane, through Palouse and over the pass</a> about 5 hours May 8th of 2022, this <A HREF="https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=1mR4SlHDOMQfKvLAcqZ9DJV8EEYTVaJLM" target="_blank">map shows the route</A>.</li>
</ul>
Adam, <A HREF="https://bsky.app/profile/meandering-miles.bsky.social" target="_blank">Meandering Miles</A> (on BlueSky) LOVES to travel on his motorcycle. He also interviews motorcyclists on their trips, as <A HREF="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fAYpGdfFXfk" target="_blank">he did with me</A>, on his <A HREF="https://www.youtube.com/@meanderingmiles" target="_blank">Meandering Miles YouTube</A> page. LOTS of motorcyclists and riding adventures.
<BR><BR>
This is a list of the trips I have taken on my motorcycle ordered by date. Each trip includes a map of the route, a page for each day that shows the ride that day, the altitudes and pictures from that day. Altitudes are useful for predicting what the temperature might be and making adjustments if you have issues with altitudes. The dates are useful as a refernce to weather conditions I experienced:
<ul style="list-style-type:circle">
	<li>Various trips riding through the <a href="motorcycle_cascade_passes.html">Cascade Passes</a> in Washington State. Started in 2015<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Vacation (meandering) to <a href="motorcycle_moab_2019-05-30_-_06-14.html">Moab Utah starting May 30, 2019</a> through June 14th, 2019.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip around <a href="motorcycle_vashon_2019-08-25.html">Vashon Island on August 25, 2019</a>. Beautiful day for a ride.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>A long ride around the <a href="motorcycle_olympic_2020-05-13_thru_16.html">Olympic Peninsula to Oregon</a> and back home from May 13, 2020 to May 16. Some rain, some shine.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>A ride to <a href="motorcycle_priestlake_2020-06-20_thru_24.html">Priest Lake in Idaho</a> and back home from June 20, 2020 to June 24. A little rain, mostly shine.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Ride to the closest <a href="motorcycle_keizer_or_2020-07-03.html">In-N-Out Burger in Keizer OR</a> and back home July 3 2020. Just because.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip to attend the 80th annual Sturgis Rally August 04, 2020 Thru August 13, 2020 <a href="motorcycle_sturgissd_2020-08-04_08-13.html">to Sturgis South Dakota </a> and riding the Black Hills then back via Yellowstone and Craters Of The Moon<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip from April 28, 2021 Thru May 01, 2021 <a href="motorcycle_bendor_2021-04-28_05-01.html">to Bend, Oregon</a> and riding the hills and amongst the mountains<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip from May 11, 2021 Thru May 14, 2021 <a href="motorcycle_moscowid_2021-05-11_05-14.html">to Moscow, Idaho</a> and riding the amazing roads in the area<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip from October 2, 2021 Thru October 8, 2021 down <a href="motorcycle_hwy101_redwood_2021-10-02_thru_08.html">West Coast Highway 101</a> to the Redwood Forest / Jedediah Smith Redwoods State Park. Highway 101 is a classic ride, beautiful and of course the Rewood Forest trees are amazing.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip May 8, 2022 from Spokane, WA down <a href="motorcycle_palouse_snoqualmie_2022-05-08.html">Palouse Scenic Byway</a> and Snoqualmie Pass.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip June 10, 2022 to <a href="motorcycle_hurricane_ridge_edmonds_2022-06-10.html">Hurricane Ridge in Olympic National Park</a> and back home.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Two part trip April 22nd, 23rd 2022 and Sept 5 thru Sept 10 2022 riding <a href="motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-04-22_2022-09-05.html">the Columbia River and Selkirk Scenic loop</a> and back home.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip October 19, 2022 to <a href="motorcycle_mt_rainier_2022-10-19.html">Mt Rainier, Paradise Visitor Center</a> and back home.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip June 3-4, 2023 to <a href="motorcycle_orcas_island_2023-06-04.html">Orcas Island</a> and back home.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip July 9-13 2023 riding <a href="motorcycle_johnday_hellscanyon_2023-07-09_2023-07-13.html">down to John Day Fossil Beds, with the painted hills, and Hells Canyon, North Americas deepest Gorge</a> and back home.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip August 6, 2023 on <a href="motorcycle_mountain_loop_2023-08-06.html">Mountain Loop Highway</a> on the southern part of the road and back.<BR><BR></li>
	<li>Trip June 12, 2025 Through July 2, 20205 on <a href="motorcycle_route66_2025-06-12_07-02.html">Route 66, Trans Canadian Highway</a> through the west and midwest, then back through Canada<BR><BR>	<li>Trip July 23, 2025 Through July 28, 20205 to <a href="motorcycle_winthrop_coeurdalene_2025-07-23_07-28.html">Winthrop Coeur dAlene Lake Coeur dAlene Lake Pend Oreille</a> and back home<BR><BR></li>
</ul>
<BR><BR>
<BR><BR>
When I visit national parks I buy a metal <A HREF="https://www.bing.com/search?q=National+Park+Pin" target="_blank">National Park Pin</A> to put on my jacket on the collar and down the sleeves. Because the backing on the pin doesn't secure the pin I have a bag of <A HREF="https://www.bing.com/search?q=locking%20lapel%20pin%20backs" target="_blank">Locking Pin Backs</A> to secure them to my jacket, I *STRONGLY* suggest the locking backs that come with a wrench, but be careful, too much tightning and you might pull off the pin on the back. After attaching I have had a couple of pins break off from the front. I wended up drilling a hole through and running a wire in the front and through the coat, see the Jedediah Smith Redwoods State Park pin. That fix is holding so far:
<BR>
<IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_coat_1.jpg">
